      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General procedure for 1–9 under aerobic conditions: to Ln(NO3)3·xH2O (0.1 mmol) in methanol (10 mL) was added dippH2 (26 mg, 0.1 mmol) in methanol (10 mL). After stirring, tmeda (23.2 mg, 0.2 mmol) was added. The mixture was heated at 60 °C for 2–3 h, cooled to room temperature, insoluble solids discarded, and the filtrate crystallized by slow evaporation at room temperature with repeated filtration; crystals formed in 1–2 weeks. Hydrated Nd nitrate was prepared from Nd oxide in 50% aqueous nitric acid. Compound 1 was isolated as block-shaped crystals.",
